+# Linear fog in the PBR material path (2026-10-20)
+
+`PBR.frag.hlsl` includes `Lighting.hlsl`, which defines the shared `ApplyFog`
+contract. The legacy lit-material shader calls it after diffuse and emissive
+lighting. The PBR shader already carries view-space position in its fragment
+input and accumulates direct light, ambient light, environment reflection,
+emission, and the optional illumination-detail layer in linear scene color.
+It previously sent that color directly to the output transform, so those PBR
+surfaces did not fade into the configured system nebula.
+
+The shared fog factor measures `viewPosition.xyz`; the homogeneous `w`
+component is not camera distance. The Basic and PBR material fades use the
+same XYZ distance rule. The PBR path applies
+`ApplyFogLinear(input.viewPosition, color)` after
+those contributions and before `ToDisplayOutput`. PBR remains linear in both
+HDR and LDR modes, so this helper always converts the legacy fog color from
+sRGB. The Legacy path retains its prior `ApplyFog` behavior, including its
+LDR color handling. Both paths share the same distance-factor calculation.
+The final alpha calculation is unchanged; the depth-only shader entry point
+does not shade color and is unchanged.
+
+The repository shader compiler completed all defined permutations for
+`PBR.txt`, `Basic_FVF.txt`, and `Basic_Skinned.txt` with the bundled DXC.
+This checks the shared helper in PBR, legacy mesh, and legacy skinned shader
+families; it does not measure pixel output.
+
+This is a source-level parity correction. A fixed-camera in-game fog scene,
+material A/B, retail comparison, and supported-GPU visual review remain open.
